// src/v4/workflow/ci.dag
//
// Scope: CI pipeline AS DATA. .github/workflows/ci.yml becomes a DERIVED artifact emitted from this file. Adding a CI gate = editing this one .dag file (THESIS:226). v3's gate #98 ci_yml_hand_authority_dissolved was an open R3 gap precisely because CI YAML was hand-authored — v4 must NOT reproduce it.
// Anchor: THESIS:223-226 (meta-process modeling: "Bootstrap, CI ... modeled as .dag workflows") + v4-close-interrogation.md §3.2 (ci_workflow_modeled_as_dag) + v3 gate #98 (the gap v4 must not reproduce)
//
// Owns:
//   - CiPipeline { jobs: List<CiJob>, gates: List<CiGate> }
//   - affected-set-driven job selection: consumes lens/affected_set.dag
//     (this is what replaces scripts/detect-affected-components.sh — the
//     shell bridge dissolves once this + affected_set land)
//   - emission target: .github/workflows/ci.yml as DERIVED artifact.
//     RECONCILED (D5, see HEADER RECONCILE): NOT a direct `.dag walks
//     CiPipeline, emits YAML` projection. `CiPipeline` (this file)
//     FEEDS the ratified single-authority `Workflow` carrier; ci.yml is
//     that carrier serialized under `WorkflowRuntime = YamlStatic` via
//     `project_github_actions(CIWorkflowDag, WorkflowRuntime) ->
//     Workflow` (Shape-B emission of `Workflow`, downstream — NOT of
//     `CiPipeline`). See SINGLE-AUTHORITY SEAM + HONEST SCOPE below.
//   - C4 (operator-ratified 2026-05-15): the committed `ci.yml` MUST
//     exist on disk (GitHub reads it from the repo) yet is NOT editable
//     authority. It is a committed == emit(<ratified `Workflow`
//     carrier>) CHECKED PROJECTION, guarded by the SAME machine as A3:
//     if committed ci.yml ≠ emit(...), CI is red and the divergence is
//     conspicuous + STOP-routed. This is how feedback_no_generated_
//     code_on_disk is honored honestly — "no editable generated
//     AUTHORITY", not "no generated bytes on disk". The `.dag` is
//     authority; the file is a checked projection. RECONCILED (D5):
//     the projected source is the ratified `project_github_actions ->
//     Workflow` seam, NOT `emit(CiPipeline)` directly; the
//     checked-projection C4 state is GATED on the missing v4 counterpart
//     of that ratified substrate — until it lands the committed ci.yml
//     is the explicit interim hand-authored bridge (HONEST SCOPE OF THE
//     C4 CLAIM + TRACKED SCAFFOLD (1) below). C4 intent unchanged; only
//     the projection MECHANISM is corrected (single-authority, P1/P2).
//   - cache keys in the emitted `ci.yml` are STRUCTURAL: each cacheable
//     job's `actions/cache` key is `content_hash` (B1) of that job's
//     input subgraph, derived from the dependency graph via
//     lens/affected_set.dag — not a hand-authored `hashFiles(...)` glob.
//     GHA `actions/cache` is one emission target of that hash; a remote
//     build cache is another. The interim hand-written `hashFiles(...)`
//     keys in the committed `ci.yml` (e.g. the v2-compiler-binary cache)
//     are manual approximations of those content-hashes; emitting
//     `ci.yml` from this file replaces them with the real structural keys.
//
// Consumes:
//   - lens/affected_set.dag: job selection
//   - extdeps/process.dag: CI steps spawn subprocesses
//   - workflow/bootstrap.dag: CI runs the bootstrap chain
//
// Status: filled (declarative core — T-24 structural-gate slice). The
// CiPipeline job/gate-DAG shape + the affected-set-selection seam are
// present and v2-compile-clean. The C4 ci.yml projection is NOT a
// present property of this data — it is BLOCKED on the missing v4
// counterpart of the ratified single-authority `Workflow` carrier /
// `project_github_actions` seam, and surfaced for operator confirmation
// (see HONEST SCOPE OF THE C4 CLAIM + TRACKED SCAFFOLD (1)); the
// committed ci.yml stays the explicit interim hand-authored bridge
// meanwhile. The canonical `ci_pipeline` instance models the
// structural v2-compile gate (the existing day-1 CI gate: v2 indexes
// src/v4). The ci.yml PROJECTION body, affected-set SELECTION body, and
// the executable test/eval jobs are DEFERRED — see TRACKED SCAFFOLD.
// HEADER RECONCILE (2026-05-17, #3213, bold-hawk-201 + operator-tier
//   review actions; D5 / #3216 standing rule, #3190 precedent):
//   operator-tier BLOCKING review findings on this PR moved the body
